<article class="env-lemma" id="0840">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0840">Lemma <span data-tag="0840">71.6.12</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X' \to X$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $D_1$, $D_2$ be effective Cartier divisors on $X$. If the pullbacks of $D_1$ and $D_2$ are defined then the pullback of $D = D_1 + D_2$ is defined and $f^*D = f^*D_1 + f^*D_2$. </p>
